       object referred to by _h_a_n_d_l_e (typically obtained by an earlier call  to
       ddllooppeenn(3)  or ddllmmooppeenn(3)).  The _r_e_q_u_e_s_t argument specifies which infor‐
       mation is to be returned.  The _i_n_f_o argument is a pointer to  a  buffer
       used  to store information returned by the call; the type of this argu‐
       ment depends on _r_e_q_u_e_s_t.

       The following values are supported for _r_e_q_u_e_s_t (with the  corresponding
       type for _i_n_f_o shown in parentheses):

